course: dictionary
lesson: 9119
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and smoke is a good example. Look at the words around it to find the meaning the writer wants. «Smoke is the biggest danger» is about the grey cloud from a fire, because danger is the clue.
explain: Smoke can also be a verb, a doing word. «The chimney is smoking» means it is giving off smoke. Smoke, smokes, smoked and smoking show when the action happens: now, always, or in the past. A noun names a thing, and a verb tells you what happens.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «A girl in England put her Christmas tree lights next to curtains; they overheated and started a small fire that filled the room with smoke.» Here smoke is the danger, not something nice. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Smoke is the grey, black or white cloud that rises from something burning.
fact: As a verb, smoke can mean to give off smoke, as in «The chimney is smoking.»
fact: «Smoked salmon» is fish kept in smoke to give it flavour.
fact: Smoke is tiny bits of burnt material in the air, and it is very dangerous. In a fire, crawl low under smoke and get out.
fact: Smoking cigarettes harms the lungs and heart, and it is not for children.
exercise: «Smoke is the biggest danger.» In this sentence, smoke is a what? | *A noun, a thing | A verb, an action word | A colour | A question word
exercise: «The chimney is smoking.» What is smoking doing here? | *Giving off smoke | Failing badly | Keeping fish for flavour | Breathing in smoke from a pipe
exercise: Which phrase means a plan failed and came to nothing? | Smoke alarm | *Go up in smoke | Smoked salmon | No smoking
test: What is the best way to get out of a room full of smoke in a fire? | *Crawl low under the smoke and get out | Hide under the bed and wait | Open the window and stay in the room | Stand up tall and run through it
test: «A hookah is a tall smoking pipe with water in it.» What does smoking mean here? | Giving off smoke as a fire does | Keeping food in smoke for flavour | Warning people of a fire | *Breathing in smoke from a pipe
exam: «Burning them releases energy but also smoke and carbon dioxide.» What does smoke mean here? | A fire alarm that warns people | *The cloud given off when things burn | Breathing in cigarettes | A tasty flavour added to food
